.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt INIT 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm init
.Nd RavenBSD PID 1 service manager
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
program is the first user process started by the kernel.
It maps the boot archive from handle 1 and reads the service manifests under
.Pa /etc/services.d/ .
Each manifest is a small TOML file with the service name, executable, arguments,
environment, dependencies, restart policy and readiness mode.
.Pp
Services start in dependency order computed at boot.
A missing dependency or a dependency cycle is fatal:
.Nm
prints
.Dq svcd: <reason>
and exits 1.
A malformed manifest is reported as
.Dq svcd: <file>: <error>
and that service is skipped; if another service needs it, the missing dependency
is fatal.
.Pp
.Nm
prints
.Dq svcd: <name> up
when a service is ready,
.Dq svcd: <name> failed: <reason>
when readiness times out, and
.Dq svcd: all services up
once every required service (or a service with a restart policy other than
.Dq never )
is running.
A service that exits is restarted according to
.Va restart ,
.Va restart_delay_ms ,
.Va max_restarts
and
.Va window_ms .
When the crash-loop limit is reached,
.Nm
prints
.Dq svcd: <name> crash loop, giving up
and stops restarting it.
.Pp
.Nm
registers the
.Dq svc:
scheme.
Its directory lists the services and
.Pa svc:/<name>
returns one status line
.Dq <name> <state> <pid-or-handle> <restarts> .
See
.Xr svcctl 1 .
.Pp
When no service manifests are present,
.Nm
keeps the M1 behaviour: it prints
.Dq init: starting ,
the
.Xr uname 1
line and
.Dq init: done ,
then exits 0.
.Pp
Test mode is configured by
.Pa /etc/svcd.conf :
.Bl -tag -width "exit_when_settled"
.It Cm exit_when_exits No = Ar service
Exit with that service's status as soon as it terminates.
.It Cm exit_when_settled No = true
Once every service is up or has given up, print
.Dq svcd: settled
and exit 0 if no required service failed, otherwise 1.
.El
Unknown keys are reported as
.Dq svcd: /etc/svcd.conf: unknown key <key>
and ignored.
The normal profile has no such file, so
.Nm
runs forever.
.Pp
There are no signals yet.
.Dq STOP
drops
.Nm Ns 's
process handle for the service and stops supervising it, but the child process
keeps running until it exits by itself.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/services.d -compact
.It Pa /etc/services.d/*.toml
Service manifests.
.It Pa /etc/rc.conf
Optional
.Dq NAME_enable
and
.Dq NAME_restart
overrides.
.It Pa /etc/svcd.conf
Optional test-mode settings.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Nm
exits non-zero when the initfs, a manifest, the dependency graph or the
.Dq svc:
scheme cannot be initialised, or when a test-mode setting asks for a failure
exit.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr svcctl 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
